  "query_preview": "..\n(This afternoon through next Monday)\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW: I asked my magic 8-ball if there will \nbe any interesting weather the start of this week, the answer was \n\u201cno\u201d. For the beginning of this week, we have a large upper level \nridge dominating our flow, bringing quiet sunny weather through \nThursday. We will continue to see highs in the upper 50s/low 60s, \nas well as low temperatures in the 30s, with potential for higher \nelevation to see lows in the upper 20s. The passage of an upper \nlevel short wave trough overnight tonight will elevate our wind \ngusts up to 20mph in the northernmost portions of Nevada, however \nwinds will quickly die down as we return to our regularly \nscheduled ridge. \n\nLooking in to this weekend, starting Friday models are suggesting\na series of troughs to pass through our area. With the passage of\nthese troughs, high temperatures are expected to start dropping\ninto the upper 40s/lower 50s over the weekend, and some areas even\ndropping in to the 30s by Monday. At the same time, there are\nsigns of an atmospheric river event, which may lead to some\nprecipitation in our area. This will bring chances for rain\nshowers in the earlier portions of the weekend, and some potential\nsnow showers in the higher elevations Sunday into Monday. Right\nnow with timing so far out, there is still plenty of uncertainty\non the timing and the strength of these impacts, so we will\ncontinue to monitor model trends as we get closer to the event. \n\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: High confidence in calm sunny\nweather the remainder of the week. Moderate confidence in the\npassage of troughs this weekend, low confidence in the timing and\nimpacts. No deviations from the NBM model output.",
